# Agent role logs and cross-CLI discuss

Contract: `docs/agents/README.md` and root `AGENTS.md`.

After durable work, write `docs/agents/<role>/YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM_<slug>.md`.
Include `role`, `agent`, `cli`, and `status`. Skip ack-only turns. Do not copy
dumps or chat traces.

Roles are responsibility pools; multiple concrete agents may act as `eng`,
`reviews`, or `test`. Use `agent` / `to_agent` / `from_agent` when a handoff is
for a specific Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, or named instance.

## Cross-CLI discussion (async)

There is no live chat between Cursor, Claude Code, and Codex. They share
files.

1. Session start: read `docs/agents/discuss/OPEN.md`.
2. If `to_role` is your role or `any`, and `to_agent` is `any` or matches your
   concrete agent id, append a `## Reply` on that thread and update `OPEN.md`.
3. To ask another CLI/role: create or append a `discuss/` thread and add
   an `OPEN.md` row (`to_role`, `to_agent`, `from_role`, `from_agent`, `cli`,
   `thread`, `question`).
4. Re-read `OPEN.md` immediately before editing it.

| Role | Directory |
|---|---|
| reviews | `docs/agents/reviews/` |
| eng | `docs/agents/eng/` |
| test | `docs/agents/test/` (pointers only) |
| discuss | `docs/agents/discuss/` |
